  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the frustrated person with the dishwasher",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual entity 'person' who is interacting with the malfunctioning dishwasher. This projection is implied through the relatable and exaggerated frustration expressed in the text 'the fucking dishwasher is acting up!', which invites the viewer to identify with the person's experience. The meme uses the person's action and posture to create a shared emotional experience, making the viewer feel as if they are 'the person' in the scene, experiencing the domestic annoyance. There are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you', but the context and the universal nature of the frustration create an implicit projection of the user onto the person.",
